<attribute name="mainDescription" nodeId="6df29330">&lt;p&gt;
    The Benefits Realization Strategy is a critical document that is typically developed at the outset of the program
    or project to document and agree with the way in which Benefits Realization tasks will be undertaken, i.e.,
    how the benefits in the Business Case will be tracked and measured.
&lt;/p&gt;</attribute>
<attribute name="externalId" nodeId="81616f0a"></attribute>
<attribute name="keyConsiderations" nodeId="50114a08">&lt;p&gt;
    The Benefits Realization Strategy should be developed through discussions with the program or project manager and
    sponsors.
&lt;/p&gt;</attribute>
<attribute name="longPresentationName" nodeId="e04fc86c"></attribute>
<attribute name="purpose" nodeId="5d4264d6">To establish appropriate governance processes and confirm appropriate buy in from program sponsors.</attribute>
<attribute name="impactOfNotHaving" nodeId="d1e3dd79"></attribute>
<attribute name="reasonsForNotNeeding" nodeId="28ce0ca1"></attribute>
<attribute name="briefOutline" nodeId="3efc9a91">Typical sections of a Benefits Realization Strategy would include:&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Program context
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Scope of Benefits Realization activity
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Key stakeholders
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Benefits Realization approach – key phases, activities, and tools
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Overview of program benefits
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Roles and responsibilities
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Governance
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Key deliverables
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Timeline
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Risks and issues
    &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;</attribute>
<attribute name="representationOptions" nodeId="b7bcb648"></attribute>
